# ─── secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Figma personal access token lives here and must never be committed. A token in git
# history is compromised even after the file is deleted — revoke it in Figma → Settings →
# Security and mint a new one. `.env.example` is the committed template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# NOTE: figma.config.json is deliberately NOT ignored. It is per-project configuration with no
# secrets in it — file keys, paths, component names — and committing it is what makes the
# pipeline reproducible for everyone on the team (and in CI). The TOKEN never goes in it;
# `auth.envVar` / `auth.envFile` only name WHERE the token is read from.

# ─── dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/versions

# ─── kit output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Renders and pixel-probe scratch: regenerable from Figma at any time, and PNGs bloat a repo.
# The default render directory is outside the project (paths.renderDir), but a project that
# points it inside wants these ignored.
figma-renders/
*.figma.png
tmp/
.tmp/

# ─── logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
yarn-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ─── OS / editor noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
